\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and The Associated Press \par \uc2 500 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Job Openings Fell 418,000 To 7.4 Million Last Month\par \par \uc2 Job openings dropped to more than a three-and-a-half-year low in September, but nearly all the decline in vacancies was in the South, suggesting that Hurricanes Helene and Milton temporarily affected demand for labor.\par \par \uc2 The downbeat report from the Labor Department on Tuesday was countered by a Conference Board survey showing consumers' perceptions of the jobs market improved considerably in October. The share of consumers who viewed jobs as being ''plentiful'' rose to 35.1 percent from 31.3 percent in September.\par \par \uc2 Job openings, a measure of labor demand, were down by 418,000 to 7.443 million by the last day of September, the lowest level since January 2021, the Labor Department's Bureau of Labor Statistics said in its Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey, or JOLTS report. Vacancies plunged by 325,000 in the South. Job openings in the West, East and Northeast fell marginally. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 EARNINGS\par \par \uc2 Paxlovid Sales Jump\par \par \uc2 Lifts \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 's 3rd Quarter\par \par \uc2 A boost from Covid-19 treatment sales helped bush \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  to a better-than-expected third quarter and a higher forecast for the year.\par \par \uc2 Demand for the drugmaker's Paxlovid treatment spurred by the latest Covid wave and a U.S. national stockpile delivery led to $2.7 billion in sales for the drug, \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The company also cited sales growth from several other drugs, as total revenue climbed 31 percent to $17.7 billion in the recently completed quarter. Adjusted earnings totaled $1.06 per share.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect earnings of 61 cents per share in the third quarter on $14.92 billion in revenue, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The drugmaker said it made a one-time delivery of a million Paxlovid treatment courses to the U.S. Strategic National Stockpile in the third quarter. \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  also saw sales of its Covid vaccine Comirnaty grow 9 percent to $1.4 billion. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 Rolls-Royce and \uc2 CEZ\par \par \uc2 Sign Nuclear Reactor Deal\par \par \uc2 The Czech power company \uc2 CEZ\uc2  signed a deal Tuesday with \uc2 Rolls-Royce SMR\uc2  to form a strategic partnership to develop and deploy small modular nuclear reactors.\par \par \uc2 Under the agreement, \uc2 CEZ\uc2  will acquire a 20 percent share in \uc2 Rolls-Royce SMR\uc2 , of Britain, for which it will pay several billion Czech crowns.\par \par \uc2 CEZ\uc2  plans to build the first small modular reactor at the existing Temelin nuclear plant in the first half of the 2030s.\par \par \uc2 The partnership is expected to result in up to 3 gigawatt energy sources installed in the Czech Republic. \uc2 CEZ\uc2  will also participate in other projects by \uc2 Rolls-Royce SMR\uc2  in Europe and worldwide.\par \par \uc2 Small modular reactors can generate up to roughly one-third the amount of power of a traditional reactor. Developers say small reactors will be built faster and at a lower cost than large power reactors, scaling to fit the needs of a particular location.\par \par \uc2 ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020241030ekau0004v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
