\par\par \uc2 The Arts/Cultural Desk; SECTC\par \b \uc2 No Violations Found in Stunt Gone Awry\b0\par\par\uc2 By Derrick Bryson Taylor \par \uc2 504 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Eight people were taken to hospitals, three of them with serious injuries, in a crash on the set of ''The Pickup'' in April. A federal investigation found no health or safety violations.\par \par \uc2 An investigation into a crash that injured several crew members on the set of the movie ''The Pickup'' this year found no safety violations, federal officials said.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration\uc2  said in a statement this week that the agency's ''thorough'' investigation of the production company, Armored Film LLC, ''did not result in violations of workplace safety and health regulations.''\par \par \uc2 The investigation into the crash, which occurred at a small airport outside Atlanta on April 20, was closed last week, she said.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Amazon MGM Studios declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Eight crew members were taken to hospitals after the crash, including two who were treated for life-threatening injuries after they were ejected from a vehicle, the authorities said at the time. A third person was treated for serious injuries.\par \par \uc2 People with direct knowledge of the episode said at the time that none of the actors in the film, including Pete Davidson, Eddie Murphy and Keke Palmer, were involved in the crash.\par \par \uc2 Amazon MGM Studios has not disclosed the plot of the film, which Deadline has described as a heist comedy. No release date has been announced.\par \par \uc2 Video of the crash obtained by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  shows a red armored truck, a GMC C6, pulling up alongside a BMW X5 S.U.V. before swerving into it.\par \par \uc2 The vehicles then veer off the road and onto the grass, where the armored truck flips on top of the \uc2 BMW\uc2 . Both land upright, with the back door of the armored truck swinging open, causing one person to tumble out of it and spreading debris onto the field.\par \par \uc2 The police said that the \uc2 BMW\uc2  had one occupant, the driver, while the armored truck was carrying seven people: a driver, a front-seat passenger and five crew members who were secured in the back with belt restraints attached to the walls.\par \par \uc2 While the collision was planned, the armored truck's brush guard became entangled in the smaller vehicle's wheel well, the authorities said.\par \par \uc2 In the days after the crash, there was no consensus on whether emergency workers or an ambulance had been on the set during filming, although an ambulance was called to the scene. It is fairly standard practice to have an ambulance on set for dangerous stunts, experts said.\par \par \uc2 Sean Miller, a spokesman for the International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees, said in a statement on Thursday that the organization appreciated the work by \uc2 OSHA\uc2 's Atlanta office.\par \par \uc2 ''IATSE members are the best in the industry and work hard to ensure their safety and the safety of those around them,'' he said. ''This incident is a reminder that all workers deserve to earn a living in a safe environment.''\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020241026ekaq0003g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
