\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and Associated Press \par \uc2 470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 Spirit AeroSystems\uc2  Plans To Furlough 700 Workers\par \par \uc2 Spirit AeroSystems\uc2  told employees on Friday that it will furlough 700 workers for 21 days as an over one-month-long strike at U.S. plane maker \uc2 Boeing\uc2  eats into the supplier's cash and inventory space.\par \par \uc2 The furloughs, first reported by Reuters, will affect Spirit Aero employees working on \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's 767 and 777 wide-body jet programs. Production of those jets was halted during the strike by more than 33,000 U.S. West Coast factory workers since Sept. 13.\par \par \uc2 The furloughs follow other \uc2 Spirit\uc2  efforts to cut costs, including a hiring freeze and travel and overtime restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Spirit\uc2  said in a statement on Friday it does not have room for additional storage of the 767 and 777 fuselages it builds.\par \par \uc2 ''We recognize the impact this has on our valued teammates and their families, and we are committed to supporting them through this period,'' said \uc2 Spirit\uc2  C.E.O. \uc2 Pat Shanahan\uc2 . REUTERS\par \par \uc2 CREDIT CARDS\par \par \uc2 Amex\uc2  Earns $2.5 Billion As Spending Continues\par \par \uc2 American Express\uc2 ' third-quarter profit topped analysts' expectations as the credit card company's cardholders continue to spend, with many holding a balance.\par \par \uc2 American Express\uc2  earned $2.51 billion, or $3.49 per share, for the period ended Sept. 30. That compares with $2.45 billion, or $3.30 per share, a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 The performance beat the $3.27 per share that analysts surveyed by \uc2 Zacks Investment Research\uc2  were calling for.\par \par \uc2 Revenue totaled $16.64 billion, meeting Wall Street's estimates.\par \par \uc2 The company once again benefited from its card members -- who tend to be wealthier and less exposed to economic fluctuations -- continuing to spend on their cards, despite some economic uncertainty and the effects of inflation.\par \par \uc2 Customers spent $387.3 billion on their cards last quarter, up 6 percent from the year before. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 INTERNATIONAL\par \par \uc2 U.S. Calls Out Swiss Move On Russian Sanctions\par \par \uc2 The United States is expressing disappointment over a decision by the Swiss government not to adopt all measures in the latest round of \uc2 European Union\uc2  sanctions against Russia over its war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Ambassador Scott Miller, the top U.S. envoy in the Swiss capital, hoped that Bern will work to close a ''loophole'' that allows overseas subsidiaries to get around sanctions, which aim to punish the Russian government over President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's war in Ukraine launched in 2022.\par \par \uc2 ''It is essential we target sanctions circumvention to dent Russia the finances and materiel it needs to continue its brutal war. None of our companies should be complicit,'' Mr. Miller said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Swiss Federal Council, the executive branch, said it had decided to adopt ''most of the measures'' included in the latest EU sanctions. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020241019ekaj0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
