\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  Seeks to Raise Billions in Financing as Strike Goes On\b0\par\par\uc2 By Niraj Chokshi \par \uc2 586 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The aerospace giant said it could raise as much as $25 billion in debt or equity over the next three years, including a $10 billion line of credit.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  on Tuesday announced steps to improve its financial position as costs mounted and a strike by its largest union entered its second month.\par \par \uc2 In two regulatory filings, the company said that it could raise as much as $25 billion by selling debt or stock over the next three years and that it had entered into a $10 billion credit agreement with a group of banks, which it has not yet drawn on.\par \par \uc2 ''These are two prudent steps to support the company's access to liquidity,'' \uc2 Boeing\uc2  said in a statement. The banks are \uc2 BofA Securities\uc2 , Citibank, Goldman Sachs Lending Partners and \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The moves come days after the company revealed about $5 billion in new costs and announced a restructuring that included plans to cut 17,000 jobs, or 10 percent of its work force.\par \par \uc2 The strike, which began a month ago, is costing \uc2 Boeing\uc2  tens of millions of dollars a day, according to various estimates. Most of the workers who walked out are involved in production of commercial airplanes, bringing much of that work to a virtual halt, though one major airplane, the 787 Dreamliner, is manufactured at a nonunion factory in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Talks between the company and the union representing 33,000 striking employees, the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2 , broke down last week, with \uc2 Boeing\uc2  retracting its latest contract offer and each side blaming the other for intransigence.\par \par \uc2 Julie Su, the acting labor secretary, visited Seattle on Monday to meet with \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and the union, the union said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The strike is very likely costing \uc2 Boeing\uc2  about $1.3 billion in capital a month, according to calculations by \uc2 Sheila Kahyaoglu\uc2 , an analyst at Jefferies, the investment bank. Given those costs and its need for more debt, raising $10 billion by selling new shares would provide the company ''considerable flexibility,'' Ms. Kahyaoglu said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 S&P Global Ratings\uc2  said it was considering lowering \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's credit rating, depending on how long the strike lasts, to junk status, a downgrade that would raise \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's borrowing costs. The company's debt totals nearly $58 billion, up from about $9 billion a decade ago.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  hasn't reported an annual profit since 2018 and has been struggling since two fatal crashes of the 737 Max, the company's most popular plane, in 2018 and 2019. Those accidents cost the company billions of dollars and severely damaged its reputation. In January this year, a door panel on a 737 Max 9 jet blew open during an \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2  flight, renewing concerns about the company's planes. The \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2  has limited \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's production of Max jets until it improves production quality.\par \par \uc2 The chief executive of one of the world's largest airlines, \uc2 Tim Clark\uc2  of Emirates, said recently that \uc2 Boeing\uc2  could be forced to seek bankruptcy protection if it was not able to issue more shares to improve its financial position.\par \par \uc2 ''Unless the company is able to raise funds through a rights issue, I see an imminent investment downgrade with Chapter 11 looming on the horizon,'' Mr. Clark told The Air Current, an aerospace news publication.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's share price was up about 1 percent on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020241016ekag0003x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
